---
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import { fenixRunner } from '../../../data/fenixRunner';
import { origin } from '../../../data/site';
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { canonicalUrl } from '../../../lib/seo';
import '../../../styles/product.css';

const { legal } = fenixRunner;
---
<Layout
  title="Fenix Runner — Privacy Policy"
  description="What data the Fenix Runner watch faces, the unlock service and this website handle, and your rights."
  canonical={canonicalUrl('/FenixRunner/privacy')}
  ogImage={`${origin}/fenix-runner-icon.png`}
  preloadHero={false}
>
  <Header slot="header" />
  <article class="product legal">
    <h1>Fenix Runner — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective <time datetime={legal.effectiveDate}>{legal.effectiveLabel}</time></p>

    <section>
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>
        The Fenix Runner watch face itself collects no personal data. The trial
        and unlock versions contact one small server to learn whether a watch has
        been paid for, and that server stores a random-looking Device Code, not
        your name, email or location. Payment is handled by Creem, not by me.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Aníbal Ribeiro, Prague, Czech Republic, is the controller for the data
        described here. Contact:
        <a href={fenixRunner.supportUrl}>email@anibalribeiro.cz</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The watch face</h2>
      <p>
        Time, steps, heart rate, battery, weather and the other readings shown
        by the face come from your watch and stay on it. The face does not
        read them out, send them anywhere or build a profile. Your style, colour
        and data-slot choices are stored on the watch and in the Garmin Connect
        or Zepp app settings you already use.
      </p>
      <p>
        A version that is sold through a store, with no trial, makes no network
        requests of its own and has no licence server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Trial and unlock versions</h2>
      <p>
        These versions lock after the trial and unlock after a one-time payment.
        To do that, the watch works out a <strong>Device Code</strong>: 8
        characters taken from a one-way hash of the watch's device identifier.
        The identifier itself never leaves the watch.
      </p>
      <p>The watch sends the following to the unlock server, through your phone's connection:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the Device Code;</li>
        <li>whether the watch is already unlocked (yes or no);</li>
        <li>
          when you scan the QR code or open the buy page, the same Device Code
          in the web address.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The unlock server stores:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the time the Device Code was first seen, to track the trial;</li>
        <li>
          after a payment, the Device Code, the Creem order ID and the date, so
          the unlock can be returned and shown again;
        </li>
        <li>IDs of payment events already processed, and refund records;</li>
        <li>
          a counter per IP address, kept about two minutes, to limit abuse.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The server does not store your name, email address, payment details or
        location. Standard operating logs (event type, Device Code, time) are
        kept by the hosting provider, Cloudflare, which also sees IP addresses
        as part of serving requests.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once unlocked, the watch checks the code on the watch itself. Device
        records are kept for as long as an unlock must keep working, because
        codes sold must stay valid.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payments are processed by <a href="https://www.creem.io" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creem</a>
        as merchant of record. Creem collects and handles your payment details,
        billing country, email address and tax information under
        <a href="https://www.creem.io/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">its own privacy policy</a>.
        I can see order details in my Creem account, such as your email address
        and country, and use them to give support, process refunds and meet
        accounting obligations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        anibalribeiro.cz sets no cookies and runs no analytics or advertising
        scripts. The web host keeps ordinary server logs (IP address, page, time)
        for security and operations. If you email me, I use your message and
        address only to reply.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why I may process this data</h2>
      <p>
        To deliver what you bought and keep the unlock working (performance of a
        contract), and to prevent abuse and keep records of sales (legitimate
        interests and legal obligations).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Sharing and transfers</h2>
      <p>
        I do not sell data or use it for advertising. It is shared only with
        Creem (payments) and Cloudflare (hosting the unlock server), who may
        process it outside the EU under standard contractual safeguards. Garmin
        and Zepp/Amazfit handle what their own stores and apps collect under
        their own policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete data tied to your Device Code or
        order, to restrict or object to its use, or to receive a copy. Write to
        <a href={fenixRunner.supportUrl}>email@anibalribeiro.cz</a> and include your
        Device Code. I may need to keep payment records for accounting law.
        Deleting a paid record means an unlock can no longer be re-issued by the
        server, but codes you already hold keep working on the watch. You may
        also complain to the Czech data protection authority,
        <a href="https://www.uoou.gov.cz" rel="noopener noreferrer">Úřad pro ochranu osobních údajů</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Fenix Runner is not directed at children and I do not knowingly collect
        data from them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version appears here with a new
        effective date.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <p class="product-links">
    <a href="/FenixRunner/">About Fenix Runner</a>
    <a href="/FenixRunner/terms/">Terms</a>
  </p>
  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>
